   "find": "<figure class=\"lcp\"><p class=\"kick\">Diagnostic workup</p><div class=\"ttl\"><span><b class=\"step\">2</b>Nephritis: is the C3 low?</span></div><ol class=\"path\"><li class=\"pt\"><span class=\"when\">First</span><div class=\"tile first\"><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Urinalysis with microscopy</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Blood and protein, red cell casts, dysmorphic red cells</b><span class=\"mask\">Glomerular (nephritic) bleeding</span></p></div><i class=\"plus\" aria-label=\"and\"></i><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Creatinine, blood urea nitrogen (BUN), electrolytes</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Creatinine raised; potassium may be high</b><span class=\"mask\">AKI; a high potassium steers away from an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor</span></p></div></div></li><li class=\"pt\"><span class=\"when\">Next</span><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">C3 and C4</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Low C3, C4 normal or mildly low</b><span class=\"mask\">PSGN</span></p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Normal C3</b><span class=\"mask\">IgA nephropathy or IgA vasculitis</span></p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Low C3 and C4</b><span class=\"mask\">Suggests lupus</span></p></div></div></li><li class=\"pt\"><span class=\"when\">Supports</span><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">ASO and anti-DNase B (streptozyme)</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Elevated titers</b><span class=\"mask\">Recent group A strep; anti-DNase B is the better marker after impetigo</span></p></div></div></li><li class=\"pt\"><span class=\"when\">By branch</span><div class=\"tile\"><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">CBC with smear</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Schistocytes, low platelets</b><span class=\"mask\">HUS rather than a glomerulonephritis</span></p></div><i class=\"plus\" aria-label=\"and\"></i><div class=\"wt2\"><p class=\"tn\">Renal biopsy</p><p class=\"wr2\"><b>Generally only when atypical: C3 still low after 8 weeks or a worsening course</b><span class=\"mask\">Looks for MPGN or lupus n